Delta since v9 touching WS-D: (1) the v9 transaction-time peel budget is WITHDRAWN; the peel's cost is bounded structurally by fitting every refit's KMeans on a deterministic stride sample of at most 256 mass members (every ceil(|M|/256)-th member of M in index order) while the partition is still assigned and scored over every vector; measured as oracle item 20 (TEST-ONLY: Java probe mode "floor-sample:S" in conformance/guardiann_probe_conformance.java, spec "measures the peel on many isolated high-dimensional outliers" now 130 pinned rows = 26 shapes x 5 modes; sampling-off mutation reddens it); the peel RNG split is taken once at peel entry; (2) consumerOutcome is rewritten in Java's per-kind statement order (exits, false alarm, split/merge decision, RNG + quantizer, phase-1 re-enqueue, neighbour fetch at splitMergeConcurrency, merge classify + no-mergeable-neighbour clear, fetchCoreClusters, KMeans) with four outcome values (CONSUMED, RUNS, REFUSED, REFUSED_UNLESS_ALL_NK) both callers act on; the bounce hands runTask its list, pick and POSITIONED RNG; a non-skipping delete re-reads the queue head with the target's serializable range read; new serializable-side and delete-vs-enqueue conflict fixtures; (3) two named poison keys (vectorCapability/... at entry points, vectorTask/... only in the task-execution wrapper) with registration-order commit semantics; (4) merge-side and beside-a-viable-candidate n<k populations declared; the reconcile's extra replica metadata reads declared; the merger and db.Run named as retry owners; (5) PRODUCTION FIX: CheckAnyOngoingOnlineIndexBuilds (pkg/recordlayer/indexing_heartbeat_admin.go) parses every heartbeat KEY first again, so a non-UUID key is IndexingHeartbeatKeyError (Go spec arm with the bad key before and after a live UUID heartbeat; JVM spec pins Java's ClassCastException via a new "ongoing"-only action in conformance/index_state_conformance.java; the key-parse mutation reddens the Go spec); DIVERGENCES.md entry updated; "exclusive session" wording; (6) evidence rebound to this tree: ws-d-oracle/evidence-run.txt regenerated from two uncached 21/21 runs with source hashes, README items 19 (corrected), 20, 21 (owed), 22; evidence-mutations.txt gains the floor and sampling-off mutations. NOT WS-D, same tree, own gates: RFC-257 WS-J (literal-carrier fix in pkg/relational/core/query/ddl/generator.go literalKeyCarrier + expr/walk.go INT entry size + pkg/recordlayer/long_arithmetic_function.go Java getNullableLong widening; WS-J oracle v2 with harvest census, structural isolation runs and 466 pins in conformance/testdata/rfc257/wsj_java_pins.json), WS-E; out of scope except where they touch WS-D claims. No WS-D production code exists beyond (5).
